  "note": "Municipal elections, 17 May 1961; Central Ward was the only contest. West Ward was settled at the withdrawals (Belfast News-Letter, 5 May 1961, p. 10). East Ward (seven seats) was uncontested, but its members are not printed in the sources searched, so it is not recorded. Thomas Corrigan and James Donnelly were retiring councillors; J. McCrea, James Corrigan and Peter Donnelly were the other Nationalist nominees, and Joe Murphy and Brian Morrison, 'who did not receive Nationalist nomination, are standing as Independents' (Irish News, 4 May 1961, p. 7). No labels are printed per candidate. Returned unopposed."
